Regarding the handling of keys near the end of animations, this is a minor breaking change where the key was previously processed twice or more in particular case, but will now correctly be processed only once. However, the case extracting root motion via `TimeScale=0` and set `TimeSeek` by script in AnimationTree has been inverted since version 4.3, fixing this is a slightly larger breaking change (although **it doesn't affect general root motion case**, the case using TimeSeek for root motion is only affected). In most cases, since movement is on a single axis, simply inverting sign should suffice. While there is no migration path for cases with non-constant speed or changes across multiple axes, in such cases, root motion via TimeSeek would naturally cause a phenomenon where it completely fails to match the skeleton. Therefore, I assume that no projects with such a configuration actually exist.

